# Firmware headers

`settings.h` contains guarded compile-time settings and declarations. Shared
configuration storage and the DST clock are defined once in
`src/DeviceConfiguration.cpp`.

The `IndoorSensor`, `MqttTelemetry`, `DeviceNetwork`, `HttpDiagnostics`,
`WeatherService`, `StationDisplay` and `SystemHealth` headers declare their module
APIs and diagnostic data. Consumers read shared sample/diagnostic state; each
source module owns its hardware clients, timers and state updates.

`TelemetryState.h`, `WeatherJson.h` and `WeatherDeadline.h` contain policies covered
by the host tests. `WeatherTransport.h` integrates bounded verified TLS reads;
`WeatherTrust.h` supplies the public CA anchor. Font/image headers are display
assets. `version.h` supplies the firmware version and GitHub tag link.

Private configuration belongs in ignored `mysecrets.h`, copied from
`mysecrets.h.example`. OTA/provisioning credentials belong in the ignored root
`mysecret_envs.ini`. The build hook generates `device_security.h` under
`.pio/build/<profile>/private/`; never create or commit a public credential header.

See the root README.md for build, validation, OTA and recovery commands, and
LICENSE for author attribution and the MIT notice.
